# Blazor Skill

Blazor WebAssembly frontend for VanDaemon running on .NET 10. Components live in `src/Frontend/VanDaemon.Web/Pages/`. Uses MudBlazor for Material Design UI and SignalR for real-time updates from the API.

## Quick Start

### Basic Page Component with Real-Time Updates and Alerts

```razor
@page "/tanks"
@inject HttpClient Http
@inject ILogger<Tanks> Logger
@implements IAsyncDisposable

<PageTitle>Real-Time Tank Dashboard</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4">Tank Levels</MudText>

<!-- Filter by name (button-triggered, not two-way binding) -->
<MudTextField @bind-Value="_filterText" Label="Filter by name" Variant="Variant.Outlined" />
<MudButton OnClick="ApplyFilter" Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary">Filter</MudButton>

<!-- Low-level alert card (shown if any tank is below 20%, but never dismissed) -->
@if (_showLowLevelAlert)
{
    <MudCard Class="mb-4 mud-warning">
        <MudCardContent>
            <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning">
                Some tanks are below 20% capacity. Check the list below.
            </MudAlert>
        </MudCardContent>
    </MudCard>
}

@if (_tanks is null)
{
    <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" />
}
else
{
    @foreach (var tank in _filteredTanks)
    {
        <MudCard Class="mb-4">
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudText>@tank.Name: @tank.CurrentLevel%</MudText>
            </MudCardContent>
        </MudCard>
    }
}

@code {
    private List<Tank>? _tanks;
    private List<Tank> _filteredTanks = new();
    private string _filterText = string.Empty;
    private bool _showLowLevelAlert;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _tanks = await Http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Tank>>("api/tanks");
        _filteredTanks = new List<Tank>(_tanks ?? new());
        CheckLowLevel();
        await ConnectSignalR();
    }

    private async Task ConnectSignalR()
    {
        // Assume HubConnection is injected elsewhere
        HubConnection.On<Guid, double, string>("TankLevelUpdated",
            (id, level, name) =>
            {
                var tank = _tanks?.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == id);
                if (tank is not null)
                {
                    tank.CurrentLevel = level;
                    // Update the alert flag only on first low level (no auto-dismiss)
                    if (level < 20 && !_showLowLevelAlert)
                    {
                        _showLowLevelAlert = true;
                    }
                    InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
                }
            });

        await HubConnection.InvokeAsync("SubscribeToTanks");
    }

    private void ApplyFilter()
    {
        // Filter only on button click
        if (_tanks is not null)
        {
            _filteredTanks = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_filterText)
                ? new List<Tank>(_tanks)
                : _tanks.Where(t => t.Name.Contains(_filterText, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)).ToList();
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    private void CheckLowLevel()
    {
        if (_tanks is not null && _tanks.Any(t => t.CurrentLevel < 20))
        {
            _showLowLevelAlert = true;
        }
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        HubConnection.Remove("TankLevelUpdated");
    }
}
```

### Notes on the Example

- The alert card appears when any tank drops below 20% but **never auto-dismisses** — it only disappears on page reload or full reinitialization.
- Filtering is **not** two-way binding; it only updates when the "Filter" button is clicked.
- The `HubConnection` is assumed to be preconfigured (e.g., via DI), but the component shows a basic subscription pattern.

## Key Concepts

| Concept | Usage | Example |
|---------|-------|---------|
| Page routing | `@page "/path"` directive | `@page "/tanks"` |
| DI injection | `@inject` directive | `@inject HttpClient Http` |
| State updates | Call `StateHasChanged()` | After SignalR callback |
| Event binding | `@onclick`, `@onchange` | `@onclick="ApplyFilter"` |
| One-way data flow | `@bind-Value` used with manual refresh | `@bind-Value="_filterText"` (no automatic re-render on change) |

## Common Patterns

### Conditional Rendering with Loading State

**When:** Fetching data on component initialization

```razor
@if (_isLoading)
{
    <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" />
}
else if (_error is not null)
{
    <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Error">@_error</MudAlert>
}
else
{
    <!-- Render data -->
}
```

### SignalR Subscription with Manual State Toggle

**When:** You need to show a persistent alert without auto-dismiss

```razor
HubConnection.On<Guid, double>("TankLevelUpdated", (id, level) =>
{
    if (level < 20 && !_alertShown)
    {
        _alertShown = true;
        InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }
});
```

